# TCPShield edge IPs — OFFLINE BASELINE ONLY.
# The live ranges are fetched automatically from TCPShield on startup and
# every 6 hours after that (https://tcpshield.com/v4/ and
# https://tcpshield.com/v4-cf/), and the last fetched set is cached in
# plugins/TCPShield/tcpshield-ips.fetched. This file is only used when the
# ranges have never been fetched (e.g. no network on first boot). If
# TCPShield publishes a new range, the plugin picks it up by itself — you
# do not need to edit anything here.
#
# To add an extra range of your own, create your own file in
# plugins/TCPShield/proxy-whitelist/ (one CIDR per line). Files there are
# always honoured on top of the fetched ranges. Lines starting with '#'
# and blank lines are ignored.
#
# Sources, as fetched 2026-11-07:
#   IPv4: https://tcpshield.com/v4/
#   IPv4 via Cloudflare-fronted edges: https://tcpshield.com/v4-cf/
#   IPv6: TCPShield AS64199 (2602:fa78::/40); tcpshield.com publishes no v6 list.
